From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anton Izmailov <wapgear4@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 15:34:26 +0200
Subject: fix: ignore cursor updates from click-through windows

Electron forwards mouse movement to click-through windows so their contents can observe hover and mouseleave events. Those windows must not select the shared desktop cursor, otherwise their cursor competes with the underlying window and flickers.

Add a per-root cursor suppression property and honor it in the event filter, Views cursor selection and renderer cursor updates. Keep cached cursor values and the CursorClient attached so forwarding and pointer-lock bookkeeping remain intact.

These selection paths run inside Chromium before native cursor changes, so an Electron HWND subclass cannot suppress them all. Remove this patch when upstream Aura provides equivalent per-root cursor suppression. Regression coverage exercises all three paths, event delivery, restoration and shared cursor state.

Fixes electron/electron#35414

